### Notes (why no scores)

- NVIDIA's own blog and newsroom state plainly: "Super VL and Bolt 74B-A9B are available now, with Bolt E4B coming Oct. 23." (https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/nemotron-3-5-super-vl/)
- Multiple outlets (Yahoo Finance, VentureBeat, News.az, tech-insider.org) repeat the 2026-10-23 date and note that NVIDIA published no benchmark scores for the E4B, so performance claims remain unconfirmed pending release and independent testing.
- The sibling Nemotron 3.5 Bolt 74B-A9B 24GB (a separate, released model) has its own technical report and benchmarks — but those belong to a different product and must not be attributed to the E4B.
- As of the run date the E4B is a documented absence: an announced product with no measurable artifact.

No normalized 1–100 scores are assigned.

